    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>’s protest against the sale of indulgences in 1517, the Reformation broke the unity of Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and created Lutheran, Reformed, Anglican and Anabaptist churches.</li><li>Its teachers held that sinners are saved by God’s grace through faith alone, that scripture is the highest authority in the Church and that all believers share in one priesthood.</li><li>Taken up or resisted by princes and cities, it became bound up with politics and war, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> of 1648 ended the wars of religion in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The name Protestant comes from a protest: at the Diet of Speyer in 1529 six princes and fourteen imperial cities formally protested against the majority’s decision to restore the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-worms">Edict of Worms</a> against Luther’s teaching.</p></aside>
    </section>

